 "findings": [
  "file-menu-render-bug: the File-tab click alone paints NOTHING (.prese-file-menu-panel stayed display:none); the panel only renders on the next App-observer re-render, which this census triggers with a REAL F5 (start presentation) + Escape (end) — the App root observer reads presentationStore.isPresenting, the Viewport that owns the panel does not observe isFileMenuOpen/activeFileMenuPanel (slide twin of the documented word/sheet File-menu bug; typing into the slide's contentEditable placeholder does NOT mark the doc modified, so the sheet's keystroke trick has no slide equivalent). Every dialog pane below is censused through that side channel, one fresh page per entry, because the pane switch needs its own re-render",
  "file-menu-no-close: a real click on the now-visible Back entry flips isFileMenuOpen in the store but the panel STAYS painted (block) — the same missing-observer re-render that made the File-tab click paint nothing also makes the menu impossible to close for the user",
  "file-menu-dead-entries: 3 dialog-declaring entries reach no dialog surface (Save as...[file-menu-panel:none], Rename...[file-menu-panel:none], Version History...[menu stayed open but the entry activated no pane and no <dialog> — a dialog-declaring entry whose pane this build never renders]) — they either close the menu (non-pane action) or declare a pane the build never renders",
